From: Plain Browser
Subject: [ui] Settings > Privacy and security: the list of sites with protections off

Category: 60-ui. A section under "Site settings" on chrome://settings/privacy lists
plainbrowser.shields.exceptions (the per-site exception list of 60-ui/0005) with a remove button per site
and an Add dialog. The element is new (privacy_page/plainbrowser_shields_exceptions.*, Polymer like the
page around it) and edits the pref through settingsPrivate, which needs the pref in prefs_util.cc's
allowlist. Entries are stored as typed; ShieldsService rewrites them as eTLD+1 sites. Strings come from
//plainbrowser/shields (AddSettingsStrings, strings in 60-ui/0008).
---
